WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.229 --> 00:00:04.451
When war veteran Frank Castle returns home
from the horrors of battle, all he wants to

00:00:04.451 --> 00:00:06.279
do is be with his wife and kids.

00:00:06.279 --> 00:00:11.059
But after they're gunned down in a mob shootout,
Frank dedicates his life to vengeance as The

00:00:11.059 --> 00:00:14.910
Punisher: a bad man with big guns and an enviable
five o'clock shadow.

00:00:14.910 --> 00:00:19.120
The Punisher has been one of Marvel's most
compelling and complex characters for decades.

00:00:19.120 --> 00:00:23.220
For proof, here are ten Punisher facts you
may not know…

00:00:23.220 --> 00:00:24.939
The Exterminator

00:00:24.939 --> 00:00:28.830
The Punisher is best known these days for
his interactions with Daredevil, but he began

00:00:28.830 --> 00:00:31.460
his comic book career as a Spider-Man villain.

00:00:31.460 --> 00:00:36.079
In The Amazing Spider-Man #129, Punisher is
hired by The Jackal to hunt for the notorious

00:00:36.079 --> 00:00:41.340
vigilante wall-crawler, claiming that Spider-Man
had killed Norman Osborne in a previous fight…

00:00:41.340 --> 00:00:45.190
when in fact Osborne accidentally killed himself.

00:00:45.190 --> 00:00:49.270
Creator Gerry Conway always intended Frank
Castle to first appear as a villain, only

00:00:49.270 --> 00:00:51.059
to eventually become a hero.

00:00:51.059 --> 00:00:52.750
Well, an extreme anti-hero.

00:00:52.750 --> 00:00:58.210
Obviously, the two made amends before Spidey
got completely punished.

00:00:58.210 --> 00:00:59.260
The Assassin

00:00:59.260 --> 00:01:04.500
Gerry Conway, Punisher's creator, originally
wanted to name the character "The Assassin."

00:01:04.500 --> 00:01:08.670
Stan Lee vetoed that idea, thinking it had
too many harsh connotations for what was,

00:01:08.670 --> 00:01:10.730
essentially, a picture book for kids.

00:01:10.730 --> 00:01:15.690
Then Lee had an idea: years earlier he created
an unmemorable robot character named The Punisher

00:01:15.690 --> 00:01:20.650
who was one of Galactus' henchmen. Lee suggested
that Conway use the robot's name.

00:01:20.650 --> 00:01:23.770
Conway took it because, well, you don't say
no to Stan Lee.

00:01:23.770 --> 00:01:26.360
He's been the Punisher ever since.

00:01:26.360 --> 00:01:27.360
The Executioner

00:01:27.360 --> 00:01:34.790
He’s starred in over 600 books which have
sold well over 200 million copies worldwide...except

00:01:34.790 --> 00:01:35.790
that we’re not talking about the Punisher.

00:01:35.790 --> 00:01:40.450
These stats belong to Mack Bolan, a fictional
character created by Don Pendleton.

00:01:40.450 --> 00:01:44.130
And if Mack Bolan didn't exist, Punisher might
not have either.

00:01:44.130 --> 00:01:48.900
Created in 1968, Mack Bolan is a Vietnam vet
who comes home from war, only to watch his

00:01:48.900 --> 00:01:53.570
family die right before his eyes at the hands
of the mafia, which sparks a lifelong obsession

00:01:53.570 --> 00:01:54.700
with vengeance.

00:01:54.700 --> 00:01:59.820
He earns the nickname The Executioner, drives
around in a weapon-filled van, and keeps a

00:01:59.820 --> 00:02:00.970
“War Journal”.

00:02:00.970 --> 00:02:05.060
Somehow, Marvel hasn't been sued into oblivion
for copyright infringement.

00:02:05.060 --> 00:02:07.510
Archie &amp; Eminem get Punished

00:02:07.510 --> 00:02:12.930
The Punisher is one of those characters who's
great on his own, but even better in a team-up...like

00:02:12.930 --> 00:02:16.599
that time he saved Eminem from an assassin
hired by a group of parents who hated his

00:02:16.599 --> 00:02:17.599
music.

00:02:17.599 --> 00:02:22.551
Published in 2009 in a two-part miniseries
creatively called Eminem/The Punisher, Frank

00:02:22.551 --> 00:02:25.840
introduces himself by killing Eminem's entourage.

00:02:25.840 --> 00:02:30.829
Later Eminem takes a chainsaw to the villain
Barracuda, and everything was just as violent

00:02:30.829 --> 00:02:32.129
as you’d expect.

00:02:32.129 --> 00:02:37.739
As strange at it was, it all seemed natural
compared to 1994's Archie meets The Punisher,

00:02:37.739 --> 00:02:41.950
where our anti-hero chases a drug dealer to
squeaky clean Riverdale.

00:02:41.950 --> 00:02:47.299
Of course, the drug dealer looks almost exactly
like Archie, so cue the comical mix-ups and

00:02:47.299 --> 00:02:48.390
mishaps!

00:02:48.390 --> 00:02:53.640
The fun and games end when the drug dealer
kidnaps Veronica, but not to worry: Punisher

00:02:53.640 --> 00:02:58.409
saves the day, and even sticks around to chaperone
the school dance.

00:02:58.409 --> 00:02:59.579
Bombing the box office

00:02:59.579 --> 00:03:04.969
Punisher has had three big-screen adaptations,
and two of them were massive financial disasters.

00:03:04.969 --> 00:03:10.999
2008’s Punisher: War Zone and the 1989 Dolph
Lundgren Punisher movie are the biggest bombs

00:03:10.999 --> 00:03:12.719
in Marvel movie history.

00:03:12.719 --> 00:03:14.329
How big, you say?

00:03:14.329 --> 00:03:19.329
Even bigger than Howard the Duck, a movie
universally regarded as one of the worst of

00:03:19.329 --> 00:03:20.450
all time.

00:03:20.450 --> 00:03:23.390
"No one laughs at a master of Quack-Fu!"

00:03:23.390 --> 00:03:25.749
Yes.

00:03:25.749 --> 00:03:27.489
Even worse than that.

00:03:27.489 --> 00:03:29.079
Dirty laundry

00:03:29.079 --> 00:03:32.930
Tom Jane turned down the role of the Punisher
a couple of times because he didn't see himself

00:03:32.930 --> 00:03:37.730
as a hero, but after finally playing him in
2004, he was hooked.

00:03:37.730 --> 00:03:41.530
He walked away from the proposed sequel due
to creative differences, but he loved playing

00:03:41.530 --> 00:03:46.370
the character so much that he starred in an
independent Punisher short film called "Dirty

00:03:46.370 --> 00:03:47.370
Laundry."

00:03:47.370 --> 00:03:50.790
Even washing black T-shirts is a bloody adventure
for Punisher.

00:03:50.790 --> 00:03:53.569
Captain America's secret admirer

00:03:53.569 --> 00:03:57.030
Punisher doesn't really care about anyone
in the Marvel universe…with the exception

00:03:57.030 --> 00:03:58.870
of Captain America.

00:03:58.870 --> 00:04:02.860
Cap was a fellow soldier, and the pureness
of his moral compass is unrivaled.

00:04:02.860 --> 00:04:07.099
Punisher actually respects Cap so much that
Punisher has at times outright refused to

00:04:07.099 --> 00:04:08.099
fight him.

00:04:08.099 --> 00:04:11.680
When Captain America was temporarily dead
in the comics, Punisher changed his costume

00:04:11.680 --> 00:04:15.340
to a red-white-and-blue theme to honor his
fallen hero.

00:04:15.340 --> 00:04:17.950
Frank Castle kills everything

00:04:17.950 --> 00:04:23.230
In a one-shot, alternate-universe comic titled
Punisher Kills the Marvel Universe, the Punisher

00:04:23.230 --> 00:04:25.360
did, well, just that.

00:04:25.360 --> 00:04:29.750
In this “What If?”-type tale, Castle's
wife and kids are killed during a fierce superhero

00:04:29.750 --> 00:04:30.750
battle.

00:04:30.750 --> 00:04:35.420
Punisher kills Cyclops on the spot for his
mistake, which gets Punisher locked away...except

00:04:35.420 --> 00:04:39.160
on the way to the prison, he meets a group
of others who were disfigured during the Marvel

00:04:39.160 --> 00:04:42.010
Universe’s countless destructive superhero
fights.

00:04:42.010 --> 00:04:46.500
Frank Castle gets everything he needs to kill
every last character in the Marvel universe,

00:04:46.500 --> 00:04:48.420
saving Daredevil for last.

00:04:48.420 --> 00:04:52.040
When the deed is done, Punisher turns the
gun onto himself.

00:04:52.040 --> 00:04:55.090
But it’s not just super-humans that he’s
got it in for.

00:04:55.090 --> 00:04:59.160
In Punisher: The End, another non-canon story,
Frank Castle is one of the last remaining

00:04:59.160 --> 00:05:01.890
humans on earth after a nuclear holocaust.

00:05:01.890 --> 00:05:06.000
Frank tracks down the last survivors to kill
them, since they were the ones responsible

00:05:06.000 --> 00:05:07.950
for the destruction of the human race.

00:05:07.950 --> 00:05:13.130
Again, Punisher kills everyone, and then chooses
himself as his final victim, setting himself

00:05:13.130 --> 00:05:18.630
on fire and wandering into the wasteland,
finally ending humanity's cycle of violence,

00:05:18.630 --> 00:05:19.630
once and for all.

00:05:19.630 --> 00:05:21.130
So, how does all of this add up?

00:05:21.130 --> 00:05:25.150
Well, in 2011, Marvel Comics editor Stephen
Wacker crunched the numbers.

00:05:25.150 --> 00:05:30.990
From 1974 to 2011, Punisher had killed exactly
48,502 people.

00:05:30.990 --> 00:05:32.199
Yeah.

00:05:32.199 --> 00:05:33.940
He's kind of a monster.

00:05:33.940 --> 00:05:35.310
In fact...

00:05:35.310 --> 00:05:37.580
He's literally a monster

00:05:37.580 --> 00:05:42.120
Punisher has been killed and resurrected as
monstrous versions of his former self—not

00:05:42.120 --> 00:05:43.680
once, but twice.

00:05:43.680 --> 00:05:48.330
In the late-'90s mini-series Punisher: Purgatory,
Frank Castle kills himself and is brought

00:05:48.330 --> 00:05:53.300
back to life as a demon hunter with two guns
that fire heavenly power...or something like

00:05:53.300 --> 00:05:54.300
that.

00:05:54.300 --> 00:05:58.560
Then in 2010, after being dismembered by Wolverine's
son, Punisher's body parts fall into the hands

00:05:58.560 --> 00:06:03.190
of the vampire and Dave Navarro look-alike
Morbius, who re-assembles Frank Castle and

00:06:03.190 --> 00:06:06.620
imbues his corpse with life...turning him
into Franken-Castle.

00:06:06.620 --> 00:06:09.780
Truly, one of the best comic book names ever.

00:06:09.780 --> 00:06:11.830
Except for maybe Fin Fang Foom.

00:06:11.830 --> 00:06:13.520
Iconic

00:06:13.520 --> 00:06:17.520
The Punisher's skull logo means more to people
in real-life than it does to him.

00:06:17.520 --> 00:06:21.130
Hundreds of Iraqi soldiers wear the Punisher's
signature skull somewhere on their gear.

00:06:21.130 --> 00:06:24.280
It's a symbol they've chosen to represent
their fight against ISIS.

00:06:24.280 --> 00:06:28.180
The trend has been going on for a while, but
it was reinforced by Chris Kyle, the subject

00:06:28.180 --> 00:06:31.980
of the movie American Sniper, who wore the
symbol during his tour of duty.

00:06:31.980 --> 00:06:35.650
That cartoony, elongated skull has become
a definitive rallying cry for anti-terror

00:06:35.650 --> 00:06:37.490
forces in the Middle East.

00:06:37.490 --> 00:06:39.150
Frank Castle would be proud.

00:06:39.150 --> 00:06:40.330
Thanks for watching!

00:06:40.330 --> 00:06:43.420
Subscribe to our YouTube channel to watch
more videos like the one you just saw.

00:06:43.420 --> 00:06:46.302
And leave us a comment to let us know what
Punisher facts you would've wanted to see

00:06:46.302 --> 00:06:46.870
on the list...

